                     /inference="EXISTENCE: similar to AA
                     sequence:SwissProt:P07860.1"
                     /note="sigma factors are initiation factors that promote
                     the attachment of RNA polymerase to specific initiation
                     sites and are then released; this sigma factor is
                     responsible for the expression of sporulation specific
                     genes and is expressed in the prespore at the onset of
                     sporulation. Interaction with spoIIAB inhibits sigma F
                     activity throughout the cell before the formation of the
                     asymmetric septum; after septation the interaction is
                     confined to the mother cell, and sigma F activity is
                     released in the prespore; Derived by automated
                     computational analysis using gene prediction method:
                     Protein Homology."
